sponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously, C leadership, A not mentioned, B conscientious.\n\nAdaptability: A not willing to further education, C not open to new ideas, B maybe okay, D hot temper.\n\nOverall, each candidate has serious concerns. Which is best? Possibly Candidate B: reliable, handles stress, good technical, but has nasty remarks (crew cooperation). That is serious. Candidate A: good decision, calm, technical, but communication difficulty and egocentric. Also serious. Candidate C: strong anticipation, leadership, technical, but show-off and not open to new ideas. Could be mitigated. Candidate D: problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but hot temper and know-it-all.\n\nWhich concerns are most critical? Crew cooperation and communication are vital. All have issues. Which is least severe? Show-off and not open to new ideas may be less immediate safety risk than nasty remarks or hot temper. So C may still be best.\n\nThus I will support Agent 1's recommendation for Candidate C, but note concerns and suggest we need to probe adaptability further. Provide evidence: anticipate dangerous situations, leadership qualities. Also mention concerns: show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nThus my public message: I agree with Agent 1, recommend C, explain why.\n\nProceed."}
